From: pVisor contributors
Subject: [PATCH] sched/idle: negotiate fixed dual-vCPU handoff with host rendezvous

ABI v3 supplies idle evidence. Each CPU reports its own programmed clockevent;
the host parks that CPU, waits for both CPUs, then rechecks both in-kernel
APIC interrupt states before publishing a whole-VM offer. No partial offer
permits VM pause. CPU topology must be fixed; hotplug cannot authorize a lease.
The single-CPU PSI and TX-watchdog deferrals remain disabled on two CPUs.
ABI v2 remains unchanged for the single-CPU profile.

--- a/kernel/sched/idle.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/idle.c
@@ -180,9 +180,15 @@
 {
 	s64 delta;
 	ktime_t next;
+	unsigned int cpus = num_possible_cpus();
+	u32 abi;
 
-	if (!pvisor_idle_enabled || num_online_cpus() != 1 ||
-	    inl(0x5050) != 0x50564902)
+	if (!pvisor_idle_enabled || (cpus != 1 && cpus != 2) ||
+	    num_online_cpus() != cpus)
+		return false;
+	/* CPU identity is supplied by the VMM's KVM vCPU, not guest input. */
+	abi = cpus == 1 ? 0x50564902 : 0x50564903;
+	if (inl(0x5050) != abi)
 		return false;
 
 	/* IRQs remain disabled throughout the handoff. The VMM anchors time
